## First exact analytic residual

`RANKONE-BEZOUT-AFFINE-ELLIOTT5D45`

This is the primitive `g=s=1` child of the earlier
`PURE5-DP-DOUBLEGCD-BEZOUT-LINE45` residual, written in its canonical
rank-one affine form rather than as a renamed escape.

The exact parity carrier in the clean squarefree cell is exposed by

`beta_DP(n) = -mu(n) L_DP(n)`,

so the remaining primitive correlation contains literal
`mu(A_t) mu(A_{t+k})`, the actual large-prime selectors, and the five-fold
centred defect coefficient.

